<title>NETHERLANDS: KLM steps up flights frequency to Surinam.</title>
<headline>KLM steps up flights frequency to Surinam.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Flag carrier KLM Royal Dutch Airlines NV said on Tuesday it and Surinam's airline SLM would step up the frequency of return flights between Amsterdam and Paramaribo to three per week from two, starting May 14.</p>
<p>KLM and SLM have been maintaining a twice-per-week service between the Dutch and Surinamese capitals since March 1993. KLM said the strong increase of demand for transport outside of the peak periods justified an increase of the number of flights.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
